#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084061} :activity/id #uuid "da88a97d-6c4e-5299-b921-71200664bd9d" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049474 :topic/id #uuid "f80da52a-4a96-5269-8885-c600a798d61e" :topic/math-academy-id 790} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084061 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084526 :tutorial/content "Let's plot the graph of ![](images/e3/e31f27c483c52d7933201e37d1f6020c20d7903402be16f28ffd407c7f3db93a.svg). According to the algebraic definition of absolute value, we have\n![](images/eb/ebc6cc8f3964043ffa2ff15f7e3501222794753f30577e4b71037efb2e4ffa30.svg)\nSo, the left-hand branch of the graph is the function ![](images/8f/8f96aa73ce843c7815a1fed6bf3f3774a173cfa4d56f13e1f3a8c48d53cd7097.svg), and the right-hand branch is ![](images/23/238e977be23f692486c8bf68f6b40255435b3d1796cc50d260a014a8c670be7b.svg):\n\n![](images/60/60ad4dfdb6086f20f5137c5b4ac4905e55d5697ec4cf31575bf79be5fd408e0c.png)\n\nNotice that the graph has a sharp corner at ![](images/c1/c1e8c20213b45135f50bdc8d4544220f7b0f943ff3ca49439660c86d017e789f.svg) We call this point the **vertex** or the **minimum point.**\n\nWe can apply **horizontal** and **vertical translations** to the graph of ![](images/e3/e31f27c483c52d7933201e37d1f6020c20d7903402be16f28ffd407c7f3db93a.svg).\n\n- The graph of ![](images/91/91c9b5c48d46f81336e889febab90a9027a96accef8626bd0743ca81042f25b8.svg) is a **vertical translation** of the absolute value graph ![](images/0c/0cb4d1ae0c2e2451edd095b9dbcca94222e8ef0514db46745a2acce4b617d78e.svg) It moves the graph ![](images/34/349015631ec44ef653936c85586d2c5ef56ba64392b3f92b4b92cbef3e731bc5.svg) units up.\n\n![](images/cd/cd8b826034f7c3668cacb490e0fab60daaf7c5cae63975bfa5cae9d468c7dec6.png)\n\n- The graph of ![](images/30/3016548be8be38ace3450d51a10371543820a3357b1adbf809d69c23c70f14bb.svg) is a **horizontal translation** of the absolute value graph ![](images/0c/0cb4d1ae0c2e2451edd095b9dbcca94222e8ef0514db46745a2acce4b617d78e.svg) It moves the graph ![](images/34/349015631ec44ef653936c85586d2c5ef56ba64392b3f92b4b92cbef3e731bc5.svg) units to the *right*.\n\n![](images/65/65912d2831dd525964b78a20f2a707d7d828daa2a5e2ebd0793c6b337a42e360.png)\n\nNote the following:\n\n- When drawing horizontal and vertical translations, it is easiest to transform the graph's vertex first. Then, the two branches can be drawn coming out of the vertex.\n\n- When we translate the graph ![](images/87/87f4b5227cb69bd468d75d826fe448c91ae677181f9142fcbe9bc757d0acea77.svg) the resulting curve is called the **image** of ![](images/e3/e31f27c483c52d7933201e37d1f6020c20d7903402be16f28ffd407c7f3db93a.svg) under the translation." :tutorial/id #uuid "1b8dce6a-8742-581b-80f6-e39c9943b395" :tutorial/math-academy-id 9295 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "bdb8f706-56c3-508a-a745-c4cf4b268e01" :step/math-academy-id 169443 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084062}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084062 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083189 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082947 :question/id #uuid "5a2db9be-6ef3-5466-a7cc-4e7e2b5670ec" :question/math-academy-id "e-14919"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "61ec00a6-06ae-5d78-bb1a-b06351432cc3" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049534} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049844}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083554} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083623} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506600}] :knowledge-point/title "Graphing a Vertical Translation"} :step/id #uuid "6d0878f5-845c-5163-b1ae-e72f37806b6d" :step/math-academy-id 169444 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084063}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084063 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083190 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082948 :question/id #uuid "2e688f8d-16cc-58d6-8791-538cc335ce04" :question/math-academy-id "e-14925"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "05cffafa-cfcf-5979-a413-b7d0b66dd434" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083624} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083676} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506528} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570741} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570773}] :knowledge-point/title "Graphing a Horizontal Translation"} :step/id #uuid "dfd03723-b5ce-5ca8-98bb-2b1cf56700d6" :step/math-academy-id 169447 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084064}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084064 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084528 :tutorial/content "Horizontal and vertical translations can be combined. It does not matter which we do first.\n\nIn general, the graph of $y=|x-h|+k$ is a translation of the graph $y=|x|$ by\n\n- $h$ units right, and\n\n- $k$ units up." :tutorial/id #uuid "b55739df-8b0d-5ef2-9702-d56de0246597" :tutorial/math-academy-id 9302 :tutorial/title "Combining Translations"} :step/id #uuid "3287422a-9367-5f91-9957-0152a7e772df" :step/math-academy-id 169450 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084065}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084065 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083191 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082949 :question/id #uuid "82de263c-391b-5d45-bbd6-353c31c806fc" :question/math-academy-id "e-14933"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca5dcf12-db1a-5cfc-b369-986caa8f666c" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083546} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083625} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083628} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506530} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186506595} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570706} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570714} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570739}] :knowledge-point/title "Combining Horizontal and Vertical Translations"} :step/id #uuid "09be9587-52a8-510c-841a-fe31ae2eb30e" :step/math-academy-id 169451}] :activity/title "Absolute Value Graphs" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186083468}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046647} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570848} :activity/id #uuid "b4da87d0-f5a5-50ee-a9f0-c6cb2fb5fc32" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049474 :topic/id #uuid "f80da52a-4a96-5269-8885-c600a798d61e" :topic/math-academy-id 790} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570841 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570706 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "189651b0-54f3-5292-acb1-78996d20c50d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570173} {:answer/id #uuid "80b350c2-d6af-593a-8af1-2ec69b5c8cad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570352} {:answer/id #uuid "933e034e-403a-57ae-b3fe-587b30e14b03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570383} {:answer/id #uuid "aa9212d0-88ad-5f2e-997d-59a47e64e7c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570425} {:answer/id #uuid "dc88590b-2d68-5698-b5ee-ad190de36855" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570511}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570425} :answer-field/id #uuid "7196b41d-0d52-543a-bb1d-8738e6064d5e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570631}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "17bccb94-8027-5ec1-b42e-ebe5775a61ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-15814" :question/problem "Find the minimum value of $y$ on the graph $y=|x-3|+3.$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that $y=|x-h|+k$ is a vertical translation of the absolute value graph $y=|x|$ by $h$ units right and $k$ units up.\n\nThe function $y=|x-3|+3$ has $h=3$ and $k=3.$ Therefore, it is a translation of the absolute value graph $y=|x|$ by $3$ units *right* and $3$ units *up*.\n\n![](images/d5/d5c67a156d80c6dabd832539a4912c2bdd7ef38af9735fcade7ee46e4ba66eaa.png)\n\nLooking at the graph, we can see that the minimum value of $y$ is $3.$ This occurs at the point $(3,3).$"} :step/id #uuid "878cfbc6-5471-58e8-915b-20a46b57e956" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570844}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570843 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570773 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23d06b4f-bc10-59f4-bad3-9be438d8e2e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(0,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570189} {:answer/id #uuid "3ba1fb6c-8327-51bf-8fb0-05e23abf8c83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-1,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570222} {:answer/id #uuid "4cf6e7fe-b201-5c9d-a8a4-bd5f53457d4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(1,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570259} {:answer/id #uuid "a4336403-9070-5be9-84ed-ebf6940c61a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(0,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570415} {:answer/id #uuid "e950df02-b773-5199-bf04-fc99be23ac4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(1,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570532}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570222} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0a5060b-5648-5c20-ac0c-e7491147f963" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570651}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "bc3a1a0d-0a47-5924-a45a-6ae72b37f737" :question/math-academy-id "q-78063" :question/problem "If $y=|x+1|$, what are the coordinates of the minimum point on the graph?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that $y=|x-a|$ is a horizontal translation of the absolute value graph $y=|x|$ by $a$ units right.\n\nThe function $y=|x+1|$ has $a=-1.$ Therefore, it is a horizontal translation of the absolute value graph $y=|x|$ by $1$ unit left.\n\n![](images/38/38532ccdd10c7a60f26fdf35c837376af799d7b024370e8b223cd61b7b18eb9d.png)\n\nLooking at the graph, we can see that the coordinates of the minimum point are $(-1,0).$"} :step/id #uuid "9272e140-eade-50e0-aa74-a463e9e7aca4" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570857}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570844 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570741 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d75859b-74a6-5c31-b94d-cfb3fec63748" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(-5,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570202} {:answer/id #uuid "53d0ffba-e11b-5c18-a494-dc8db0e90b44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(0,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570272} {:answer/id #uuid "7df37ea3-f56a-521e-9c32-559774529837" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(0,-5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570346} {:answer/id #uuid "96e0d1b5-5c60-5283-a61c-715d74c22923" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(0,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570388} {:answer/id #uuid "ca1bc01f-1907-59c5-ae47-53cddb450003" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(5,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570475}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570475} :answer-field/id #uuid "b93eba92-6655-5d26-b15a-6487f0a03dd6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570667}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7432d94a-3593-5858-b61c-052181b6a281" :question/math-academy-id "q-15826" :question/problem "If $y=|x-5|$, what are the coordinates of the minimum point on the graph?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that $y=|x-a|$ is a horizontal translation of the absolute value graph $y=|x|$ by $a$ units right.\n\nThe function $y=|x-5|$ has $a=5.$ Therefore, it is a horizontal translation of the absolute value graph $y=|x|$ by $5$ units right.\n\n![](images/ca/ca70d305bb0da32441611d879ca2a4a2453b38e951b448964b5d48f01fa33e28.png)\n\nLooking at the graph, we can see that the coordinates of the minimum point are $(5,0).$"} :step/id #uuid "9437c58f-f80b-51f5-a33f-6de7c5ebdc3a" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570843}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570848 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570739 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04656707-2a2c-5ffa-bbcb-9540a7b1d0c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570130} {:answer/id #uuid "091b549b-9482-5c9d-99a3-414abc46226c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570138} {:answer/id #uuid "96ce8727-2f4f-5e50-b3b2-f6937e57145d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570387} {:answer/id #uuid "9cff91ed-11f3-5a4c-b5a3-c02c22d2774b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570402} {:answer/id #uuid "e8201c4f-d73c-5a75-aee0-069d79e730fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570529}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570138} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f1dab20-875a-5ecd-83ee-e9779ffd70fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570604}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6dff94b8-5d8c-56b5-9363-d9107e29b4d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-15811" :question/problem "Find the minimum value of $y$ on the graph $y=|x+4|-1.$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that $y=|x-h|+k$ is a vertical translation of the absolute value graph $y=|x|$ by $h$ units right and $k$ units up.\n\nThe function $y=|x+4|-1$ has $h=-4$ and $k=-1.$ Therefore, it is a translation of the absolute value graph $y=|x|$ by $4$ units *left* and $1$ unit *down*.\n\n![](images/45/45411bac1f347093b8b9931e1f8f8bee4f1eb411b6256a4c56d0ba33cffe603e.png)\n\nLooking at the graph, we can see that the minimum value of $y$ is $-1.$ This occurs at the point $(-4,-1).$"} :step/id #uuid "a2af62b9-442c-506b-9cce-b6a9e9270c22" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570841}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570857 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570714 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee5d6999-dacf-585b-9763-55851b2e5a28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570541}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570541} :answer-field/id #uuid "aecd1abd-2502-5a3e-aece-0d12a409100b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570660}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2b65f25b-10a0-5e3f-8752-11a285fdf596" :question/math-academy-id "q-222360" :question/problem "The minimum value of the function $y=|x+3|+2$ is $y=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Remember that $y=|x-h|+k$ is a vertical translation of the absolute value graph $y=|x|$ by $h$ units right and $k$ units up.\n\nThe function $y=|x+3|+2$ has $h=-3$ and $k=2.$ Therefore, it is a translation of the absolute value graph $y=|x|$ by $3$ units *left* and $2$ units *up*.\n\n![](images/81/81bace946b2fb425efa7fd7c54eb53ec353be5d9ef1516d9cf24e2c13656a60b.png)\n\nLooking at the graph, we can see that the minimum value of $y$ is $2.$"} :step/id #uuid "c6cb8059-d840-5375-a89b-c4dc968b16b1"}] :activity/title "Absolute Value Graphs" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570110}]}
